1
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,679
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:07,699 --> 00:00:12,179
Pip strokes an iron nail with Basil's magnet, again and again, always

3
00:00:12,199 --> 00:00:13,159
the same way.

4
00:00:13,429 --> 00:00:16,449
Then he holds the nail near some steel paper clips.

5
00:00:16,719 --> 00:00:17,789
What happens?

6
00:00:17,847 --> 00:00:19,367
One, nothing happens.

7
00:00:20,587 --> 00:00:22,667
Two, the nail attracts the clips.

8
00:00:24,153 --> 00:00:25,663
Hold on to your answer!

9
00:00:27,535 --> 00:00:30,575
Today, we find out what the strokes did to Pip's nail!

10
00:00:30,778 --> 00:00:33,798
Our fishing game needs three hooks to catch paper fish.

11
00:00:33,828 --> 00:00:35,818
But we only have one magnet!

12
00:00:36,098 --> 00:00:38,728
A little woodpecker is hiding in this video.

13
00:00:38,988 --> 00:00:40,218
Can you spot it?

14
00:00:40,339 --> 00:00:42,069
Listen for a tap, tap, tap!

15
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:43,580
You against the Buddies!

16
00:00:43,850 --> 00:00:45,700
Lock in first with your fingers.

17
00:00:45,970 --> 00:00:47,800
One finger for every point.

18
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:49,701
Today you'll learn:

19
00:00:49,902 --> 00:00:51,792
What magnetised means.

20
00:00:51,989 --> 00:00:53,539
How to test the nail.

21
00:00:53,743 --> 00:00:55,543
What can be magnetised.

22
00:00:56,045 --> 00:00:56,985
Are you ready?

23
00:00:57,425 --> 00:00:58,195
Three!

24
00:00:58,575 --> 00:00:59,235
Two!

25
00:00:59,605 --> 00:01:00,255
One!

26
00:01:00,675 --> 00:01:01,395
Go!

27
00:01:02,784 --> 00:01:03,674
Round one!

28
00:01:03,964 --> 00:01:06,434
Pip's nail meets the steel paper clips.

29
00:01:06,714 --> 00:01:07,774
What happens?

30
00:01:08,044 --> 00:01:09,364
Show me your fingers!

31
00:01:12,838 --> 00:01:13,818
Locked in!

32
00:01:13,946 --> 00:01:14,616
One.

33
00:01:14,766 --> 00:01:17,516
The magnet has gone away now, so the nail is just a

34
00:01:17,536 --> 00:01:18,606
nail again.

35
00:01:18,657 --> 00:01:23,327
Two. An iron nail is made of a magnetic material, so it always

36
00:01:23,347 --> 00:01:24,917
attracts steel clips.

37
00:01:24,969 --> 00:01:25,599
Two!

38
00:01:25,729 --> 00:01:29,139
The hardware shop uncle strokes his screwdriver with a magnet.

39
00:01:29,319 --> 00:01:31,009
Then it holds tiny screws!

40
00:01:31,282 --> 00:01:32,572
Be the iron nail!

41
00:01:32,902 --> 00:01:33,882
Shrink down.

42
00:01:34,162 --> 00:01:35,092
Quietly.

43
00:01:37,378 --> 00:01:40,548
You are an iron nail, lying on a wooden table.

44
00:01:41,338 --> 00:01:44,638
A giant magnet comes down, onto your flat head.

45
00:01:45,148 --> 00:01:48,288
It slides all the way along you, to your sharp tip.

46
00:01:49,058 --> 00:01:52,018
Then it lifts up and away, and comes back down on your

47
00:01:52,038 --> 00:01:52,668
head.

48
00:01:53,179 --> 00:01:55,909
Again, and again, always the same way.

49
00:01:56,699 --> 00:02:00,049
Now a giant hand carries you down to the steel clips.

50
00:02:00,819 --> 00:02:03,059
They jump up, and cling to your tip!

51
00:02:04,707 --> 00:02:07,637
The answer is two: the nail attracts the clips!

52
00:02:07,887 --> 00:02:09,467
Did you show two fingers?

53
00:02:09,737 --> 00:02:11,108
Put one finger up!

54
00:02:11,128 --> 00:02:14,028
The stroke method is a way to make a magnet that uses

55
00:02:14,048 --> 00:02:18,488
a strong magnet, such as my bar magnet stroking Pip's iron nail!

56
00:02:19,217 --> 00:02:22,877
See? Iron nails always attract steel clips!

57
00:02:23,526 --> 00:02:24,676
Look closer.

58
00:02:25,266 --> 00:02:27,596
Here is a new nail from the same bag.

59
00:02:28,176 --> 00:02:29,704
Nobody has stroked it.

60
00:02:29,724 --> 00:02:31,654
Hold it over the steel clips.

61
00:02:32,234 --> 00:02:33,935
Not one clip jumps up.

62
00:02:33,955 --> 00:02:39,015
Basil's magnet pulls the new nail, because iron is a magnetic material.

63
00:02:39,575 --> 00:02:41,785
But the new nail is not a magnet.

64
00:02:41,805 --> 00:02:45,405
Now Pip's nail, with the magnet shut away in its box.

65
00:02:45,985 --> 00:02:47,285
The clips jump up!

66
00:02:47,875 --> 00:02:50,625
Pip's nail has been magnetised.

67
00:02:51,415 --> 00:02:55,255
Magnetised means made into a magnet, such as Pip's nail after all

68
00:02:55,275 --> 00:02:56,395
those strokes!

69
00:02:58,810 --> 00:03:01,900
Pip had the right card for the wrong reason, so the Buddies

70
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:03,020
get no point.

71
00:03:03,378 --> 00:03:04,538
Say it with me!

72
00:03:05,244 --> 00:03:08,564
When a magnetic object becomes a magnet, we say that it has

73
00:03:08,584 --> 00:03:10,074
been magnetised.

74
00:03:12,702 --> 00:03:13,602
My turn!

75
00:03:13,702 --> 00:03:16,182
I made Rod Two's hook with just one stroke.

76
00:03:16,342 --> 00:03:18,152
Look, the steel clips jump up!

77
00:03:18,276 --> 00:03:19,836
Something is not right.

78
00:03:20,106 --> 00:03:22,286
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

79
00:03:22,566 --> 00:03:23,526
Hold on!

80
00:03:28,939 --> 00:03:30,069
Arms crossed?

81
00:03:30,339 --> 00:03:31,549
One finger up!

82
00:03:31,601 --> 00:03:33,441
Look where the clips are, Basil.

83
00:03:33,721 --> 00:03:36,021
They are on your magnet, not on your nail!

84
00:03:36,221 --> 00:03:38,971
Put the magnet away first, then test the nail.

85
00:03:39,100 --> 00:03:43,510
Test the magnetised iron nail by placing it near some steel clips.

86
00:03:43,790 --> 00:03:47,070
Observe if the iron nail attracts any steel clips.

87
00:03:47,807 --> 00:03:51,147
If we stroke anything enough times, it will become a magnet.

88
00:03:51,247 --> 00:03:53,067
Even my wooden chopstick!

89
00:03:53,716 --> 00:03:54,866
Look closer.

90
00:03:55,456 --> 00:03:59,946
A copper wire, aluminium foil, a wooden chopstick and a new steel

91
00:03:59,966 --> 00:04:00,916
screwdriver.

92
00:04:01,496 --> 00:04:04,651
Before stroking, none of them attracts any clips.

93
00:04:04,671 --> 00:04:08,161
Stroke each one the same way, the same number of times.

94
00:04:08,731 --> 00:04:11,914
Now only the steel screwdriver attracts the clips.

95
00:04:11,934 --> 00:04:14,905
Steel is a magnetic material, like iron.

96
00:04:14,925 --> 00:04:18,145
A magnetic object is an object that is made of a magnetic

97
00:04:18,165 --> 00:04:22,155
material, such as an iron nail or a steel screwdriver.

98
00:04:25,455 --> 00:04:26,675
Say it with me!

99
00:04:27,383 --> 00:04:30,833
We can turn a magnetic object into a magnet by stroking it

100
00:04:30,853 --> 00:04:32,393
with a strong magnet.

101
00:04:34,871 --> 00:04:36,331
Show me your score hand!

102
00:04:36,611 --> 00:04:37,641
Two fingers?

103
00:04:37,921 --> 00:04:39,291
You beat the Buddies.

104
00:04:39,571 --> 00:04:40,571
High five!

105
00:04:41,149 --> 00:04:42,699
Did you spot the woodpecker?

106
00:04:43,019 --> 00:04:46,609
It was on the handle of a broom, outside the hardware shop!

107
00:04:46,742 --> 00:04:48,222
Here is a fun fact!

108
00:04:48,302 --> 00:04:52,582
A woodpecker pecks again and again, many times every second, like super-fast

109
00:04:52,602 --> 00:04:53,412
strokes!

110
00:04:53,432 --> 00:04:56,022
And its tongue is so long, it wraps round the back of

111
00:04:56,042 --> 00:04:56,882
its head!

112
00:04:57,007 --> 00:04:58,287
Tell someone at home!

113
00:04:59,016 --> 00:05:01,216
Let's read today's key words together!

114
00:05:01,506 --> 00:05:02,266
Ready?

115
00:05:02,553 --> 00:05:03,753
Stroke method.

116
00:05:05,354 --> 00:05:06,534
Magnetised.

117
00:05:08,123 --> 00:05:09,543
Magnetic object.

118
00:05:11,424 --> 00:05:12,364
Well done!

119
00:05:13,161 --> 00:05:14,411
My way is faster!

120
00:05:14,471 --> 00:05:16,911
Back and forth, with both ends of the magnet.

121
00:05:17,001 --> 00:05:18,635
My hook will be the strongest!

122
00:05:18,655 --> 00:05:20,465
Will Basil's fast way work?

123
00:05:20,765 --> 00:05:22,345
Find out in Part Two!

124
00:05:23,503 --> 00:05:24,604
Say it with us!

125
00:05:25,404 --> 00:05:26,154
Ready?

126
00:05:26,278 --> 00:05:26,938
One!

127
00:05:27,278 --> 00:05:27,978
two!

128
00:05:28,283 --> 00:05:29,458
Now you know!
